{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015TC8mmZKSvkWBrAgSxqe4G","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"repo\":\"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-billing-app\",\"number\":854,\"kind\":\"pr\",\"title\":\"(fix) Load billing pages, forms and modals only when they open\",\"state\":\"merged\",\"author\":\"denniskigen\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-09-29T06:19:51.000Z\",\"mergedAt\":\"2026-09-29T09:05:55.000Z\",\"closedAt\":\"2026-09-29T09:05:55.000Z\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-billing-app/pull/854\",\"mergeCommit\":\"e021519623779cdf5f866fa0541aecfdbcc4aeaa\",\"syncedAt\":\"2026-10-23T18:59:47.249Z\",\"tickets\":[],\"commits\":[{\"sha\":\"e021519623779cdf5f866fa0541aecfdbcc4aeaa\",\"source\":\"merge-commit-sha\",\"verified\":true}],\"files\":[{\"path\":\"package.json\",\"additions\":1,\"deletions\":0},{\"path\":\"src/billable-services/billable-services-menu-item/item.component.tsx\",\"additions\":0,\"deletions\":18},{\"path\":\"src/billable-services/billable-services-menu-item/item.scss\",\"additions\":0,\"deletions\":14},{\"path\":\"src/index.ts\",\"additions\":32,\"deletions\":26},{\"path\":\"src/routes.json\",\"additions\":0,\"deletions\":8},{\"path\":\"yarn.lock\",\"additions\":1,\"deletions\":0}],\"body\":\"## Requirements\\n\\n- [x] This PR has a title that briefly describes the work done including the ticket number. If there is a ticket, make sure your PR title includes a [conventional commit](https://o3-docs.openmrs.org/en-US/docs/frontend-modules/contributing/#contributing-guidelines) label. See existing PR titles for inspiration.\\n- [ ] My work is based on designs, which are linked or shown either in the Jira ticket or the description below. (See also: [Styleguide](http://om.rs/o3ui))\\n- [x] My work includes tests or is validated by existing tests.\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nThis registers billing's dashboard, billable services page, bill history, visit check-in form and seven modals with `getAsyncLifecycle`, so their code only loads when they're shown. It also adds `react-router-dom` to `peerDependencies`, so billing uses the app shell's copy.\\n\\nThe Billing link renders on the home page, and with `getSyncLifecycle` everything those lifecycles import loaded as soon as the module started. So every session downloaded billing's invoice and forms, along with `zod`, `react-hook-form` and `react-to-print`, before anyone opened anything billing-related. The nav links, left panel links and patient banner tags stay synchronous because they render on other apps' pages.\\n\\nI built billing from `main` and from this branch, swapped each into a build of today's O3 `next`, and ran the same workflows as the 3.8.0 benchmark: home, the patient chart, visits, clinical forms, the order basket and patient search.\\n\\n| | `main` | This PR |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Billing code loaded when the module starts | 297 KiB | 67 KiB |\\n| Billing JS loaded across the workflows | 344 KiB | 114 KiB |\\n| Copies of `react-router-dom` loaded | 2 | 1 |\\n\\nSizes are uncompressed. The billing dashboard, billable services, the Add cash point modal, the patient chart's Billing history, and the billing fields in the Start a visit form rendered with no page errors on both builds.\\n\\n## Screenshots\\n\\n## Related Issue\\n\\n## Other\\n\\nThe patient chart side of this is openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart#3712.\\n\",\"nextOffset\":null,\"truncated\":[]}"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7b26a3ad-b8ff-4001-a027-cf0b70140137","uuid":"3451284d-8d4d-4f4e-af1d-57bdf3da6efb","timestamp":"2026-10-23T19:25:32.724Z","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"repo\":\"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-billing-app\",\"number\":854,\"kind\":\"pr\",\"title\":\"(fix) Load billing pages, forms and modals only when they open\",\"state\":\"merged\",\"author\":\"denniskigen\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-09-29T06:19:51.000Z\",\"mergedAt\":\"2026-09-29T09:05:55.000Z\",\"closedAt\":\"2026-09-29T09:05:55.000Z\",\"